# `o instanceof V` in a loop, with V a function that is constructed and that code out of sight holds: it may give V another `prototype` or a Symbol.hasInstance at any time, so the guards of the class are asked first, and the operator as written stands on their failing side
# an object with the shape of V says itself whether it stands where it was made; whatever has another shape walks its chain up to the prototype object of V
# a plain object laid between an object and the prototype object of V is taken for no other prototype, and what is done to that link later ends guards alone: so the guard of the prototype's side is asked with the others
# function V(x) { this.x = x; }  sink(V);  function isV(o, C) { return o instanceof C; }  function countV(o, C, n) { let s = 0; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) s += o instanceof C; return s; }
